                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "- Playtime: 23 minutes\n\n- Played: 2026\n\n- Context: I like quite a few Hidden Object Games.\n\n[b]Review[/b]\n\nThis is a game from 2015 that looks like something from at least a decade earlier. Gameplay consists of finding objects and sometimes using them on other objects. There's also moving things with a crane and shooting with a catapult/cannon - both of which use the same controls. And some basic puzzles.\n\nThe difficulty mainly comes from the rather poor graphics and fiddly controls. And also some moon logic. The first level/map has you collect supplies for a journey in a sack. So i clicked on the sack. It didn't work. I clicked on the water melon. It didn't work. It turns out you first collect the apples to eat, then the sack to put them in. And the watermelons are used to make fuel. Of course.\n\nSome of the dialogue is amusing but it's not enough to overcome the gameplay.",
